# Line endings are normalised to LF, in the repository and in the working copy.
#
# Without this file, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true converts every
# text file to CRLF on checkout. Git then has to rewrite all 128 files on any
# operation that touches the tree — which is why a commit of four lines in
# .gitignore produced a screen of "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings and
# then died on a file nobody had edited.
#
# LF is also what actually runs: these files are served by Cloudflare Pages and
# executed by Workers, neither of which wants CRLF, and a .sql file with CRLF
# line endings is a needless diff against every earlier migration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never touch these, never try to diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xlsm  binary
*.docx  binary
*.epub  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
